---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const platformFaqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  'mainEntity': [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'What are the main advantages of Real Color Mixer over standard digital tools?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Real Color Mixer offers three core advantages: 1) Physical Kubelka-Munk pigment physics that blend blue and yellow into vibrant green rather than muddy grey; 2) A dual-mode color wheel supporting Johannes Itten classical artist RYB and digital RGB; and 3) Real-time WCAG 2.1 AA/AAA accessibility scoring with 100% free, privacy-first access without account sign-in.'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'Who uses Real Color Mixer and what are its primary applications?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'The platform is used across five primary industries: 1) Fine artists and painters to prototype oil and acrylic mixing recipes without wasting paint; 2) UI/UX designers to create accessible palettes with legal WCAG contrast; 3) Front-end developers to generate modern CSS color-mix() code and Tailwind v4 tokens; 4) Interior decorators to test wall paint tints and undertones; and 5) Educators to teach subtractive vs additive color physics.'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'How do the Color Wheel Picker and Color Mixer tools work together?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'The two tools form an integrated workflow: First, creators use the Color Wheel Picker (/color-wheel) to establish harmonic palettes (such as complementary or triadic schemes) and test accessibility. Next, they transition to the Color Mixer (/mix) to simulate physical pigment blends with proportion sliders or generate native CSS color-mix() tokens.'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'Is Real Color Mixer free and does it require an Adobe Creative Cloud account?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Real Color Mixer is 100% free and open to all users. Unlike Adobe Color Wheel, you do not need an Adobe Creative Cloud account, subscription, or login to save, test, or export your color palettes and code snippets.'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'What export formats are supported for web and graphic designers?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Real Color Mixer supports one-click exports for Tailwind CSS v4 design tokens, CSS custom properties (:root variables), modern CSS color-mix() syntax in OKLCH, downloadable SVG palette swatches, and standard HEX / RGB / HSL values.'
      }
    }
  ]
};

const pageSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebSite',
    'name': 'Real Color Mixer',
    'url': 'https://realcolormixer.com',
    'description': 'Next-generation color science platform unifying physical Kubelka-Munk pigment optics, classical Johannes Itten Bauhaus harmonies, and modern accessible design tools.'
  },
  platformFaqSchema
];
---

<Layout
  title="Real Color Mixer - Next-Gen Color Science Suite & Paint Tools"
  description="Discover the advantages and professional uses of Real Color Mixer. Explore subtractive pigment physics, classical Bauhaus harmonies, and accessible digital color tools."
  keywords="real color mixer, color science platform, pigment physics, physical paint mixer, itten color wheel, accessible color tools, wcag contrast, css color mix"
  currentPath="/"
  schema={pageSchema}
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-white dark:bg-[#0a0a0a] py-16 sm:py-24">
    <!-- Vercel Geist Mesh Gradient Bloom -->
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden opacity-30 dark:opacity-20">
      <div class="absolute -top-[30%] left-[25%] h-[400px] w-[600px] rounded-full bg-gradient-to-tr from-[#007cf0]/40 via-[#7928ca]/30 to-[#ff0080]/30 blur-3xl"></div>
      <div class="absolute -top-[20%] right-[10%] h-[350px] w-[500px] rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-[#00dfd8]/30 via-[#f9cb28]/30 to-[#ff4d4d]/30 blur-3xl"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <!-- Eyebrow Badge -->
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#2e2e2e] bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[#141414] px-3.5 py-1 text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] shadow-2xs">
          <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#0070f3] animate-pulse"></span>
          <span>Next-Generation Color Science Platform</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
          Color science engineered for artists, designers & developers.
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] sm:text-lg">
          Stop struggling with muddy RGB averages and rigid screen-only pickers. Real Color Mixer unifies authentic <strong>Kubelka-Munk pigment physics</strong> with <strong>Johannes Itten's Bauhaus color wheel</strong> and modern <strong>WCAG 2.1 accessibility</strong>.
        </p>

        <!-- Primary CTAs -->
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/mix"
            class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#171717] dark:bg-white px-7 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:text-[#171717] shadow-xs transition-colors hover:bg-[#333333] dark:hover:bg-[#e0e0e0]"
          >
            Launch Color Mixer &rarr;
          </a>
          <a
            href="/color-wheel"
            class="inline-flex h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#333333] bg-white dark:bg-[#141414] px-7 text-sm font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] shadow-2xs transition-colors hover:bg-[#fafafa] dark:hover:bg-[#1f1f1f]"
          >
            Open Color Wheel &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Tools Showcase Grid -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 bg-white dark:bg-[#0a0a0a]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mb-12 text-center">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">Dedicated Tool Suite</span>
        <h2 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Two specialized tools. One cohesive color ecosystem.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        <!-- Card 1: /mix -->
        <a
          href="/mix"
          class="group relative flex flex-col justify-between rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-white dark:bg-[#111111] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-2xs transition-all hover:border-[#171717]/30 dark:hover:border-white/30 hover:shadow-md"
        >
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-tr from-blue-500 to-emerald-400 text-white shadow-xs">
                <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19.428 15.428a2 2 0 00-1.022-.547l-2.387-.477a6 6 0 00-3.86.517l-.318.158a6 6 0 01-3.86.517L6.05 15.21a2 2 0 00-1.806.547M8 4h8l-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 00.586 1.414l5 5c1.26 1.26.367 3.414-1.415 3.414H4.828c-1.782 0-2.674-2.154-1.414-3.414l5-5A2 2 0 009 10.172V5L8 4z" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a] group-hover:text-[#171717] dark:group-hover:text-white">/mix →</span>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white">
              Real Color Mixer Tool
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
              Simulate physical paint blending using the Kubelka-Munk theory. Blend custom hex codes or traditional artist pigment tubes with fluid weight sliders and export modern CSS color-mix() code.
            </p>

            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5 text-xs text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Physical Pigments:</strong> Blue + Yellow = Vibrant Green (#3D933E)</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>4 Blending Modes:</strong> Real Paint (RYB), OKLCH, RGB, CMYK</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Developer Ready:</strong> Native CSS color-mix() and Tailwind v4 export</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222]">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#0070f3] dark:text-[#3291ff] group-hover:underline">Open Color Mixer Tool &rarr;</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <!-- Card 2: /color-wheel -->
        <a
          href="/color-wheel"
          class="group relative flex flex-col justify-between rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-white dark:bg-[#111111] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-2xs transition-all hover:border-[#171717]/30 dark:hover:border-white/30 hover:shadow-md"
        >
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-tr from-rose-500 via-amber-400 to-indigo-500 text-white shadow-xs">
                <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M11 3.055A9.001 9.001 0 1020.945 13H11V3.055z" />
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M20.488 9H15V3.512A9.025 9.025 0 0120.488 9z" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a] group-hover:text-[#171717] dark:group-hover:text-white">/color-wheel →</span>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white">
              Color Wheel Picker Tool
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
              Interactive dual-mode color wheel. Switch seamlessly between Johannes Itten's classical Bauhaus 12-hue artist wheel and standard digital screen color wheels.
            </p>

            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5 text-xs text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Artist RYB Wheel:</strong> Red opposite Green, Blue opposite Orange</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Harmonies:</strong> Complementary, Triadic, Analogous, Tetradic</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                <span><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Real-time WCAG 2.1 contrast + Color-blind simulator</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222]">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#0070f3] dark:text-[#3291ff] group-hover:underline">Explore Color Wheel Tool &rarr;</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Competitor Comparison Section -->
  <section class="border-t border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[#0e0e0e] py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">Platform Advantages</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Real Color Mixer vs. Legacy Digital Design Tools
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
          See how our physical pigment science and open architecture compare directly against conventional screen utilities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-white dark:bg-[#111111] shadow-2xs">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <thead class="border-b border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[#171717] text-xs font-mono uppercase text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-4 sm:p-5">Feature</th>
              <th class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">Standard Screen Tools</th>
              <th class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-[#171717] dark:text-white font-bold">Real Color Mixer Suite</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#ebebeb] dark:divide-[#222222] text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Blue + Yellow Mixing Result</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 font-mono">Muddy Brown/Grey (#808040)</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-semibold font-mono">Vibrant Green (#3D933E)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Color Mixing Physics</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5">Linear Digital RGB Average</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Subtractive Kubelka-Munk (K/S) + OKLCH</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Harmonic Color Theory</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5">RGB Only (Red opposite Cyan)</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Dual Mode: Johannes Itten RYB + Digital RGB</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Account / Subscription Required</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">Frequently required for saving/syncing</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">100% Free & No Sign-In Required</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Accessibility Validation</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">None or basic external checkers</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">Real-time WCAG 2.1 AA & AAA Badges</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Tonal Scales & Steps</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">Single hex code</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Full 9-Step Tint & Shade Scale (50 to 900)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Color Vision Deficiency Simulation</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">None</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Protanopia, Deuteranopia, Tritanopia, Mono</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Code Generation</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5">Manual hex copying</td>
              <td class="p-4 sm:p-5 font-medium text-[#171717] dark:text-white">Tailwind CSS v4, CSS Vars, CSS color-mix()</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Comprehensive Editorial Guide on Uses & Advantages (1,000 words) -->
  <article class="border-t border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-white dark:bg-[#0a0a0a] py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Section Header -->
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#8f8f8f] dark:text-[#71717a]">Platform Overview & Applications</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">
          The Advantages, Science & Professional Uses of Real Color Mixer
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa]">
          How our dual-tool architecture bridges physical pigment reality with accessible modern web engineering.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Main Prose Body -->
      <div class="space-y-12 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-[#374151] dark:text-[#d1d5db]">
        
        <!-- Part 1: Why Real Color Mixer Exists -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#111827] dark:text-white">
            1. Why Real Color Mixer Exists: Beyond Digital Screen Limitations
          </h3>
          <p>
            Real Color Mixer represents a fundamental shift in how digital color tools operate. For decades, creators have had to rely on tools that treat color purely as mathematical abstractions of light on computer monitors. While additive RGB color models suit emitting pixels on a screen, they fail to replicate how colors interact physically or how human vision perceives harmony.
          </p>
          <p>
            Real Color Mixer was engineered from the ground up to solve these longstanding limitations. By unifying physical pigment optics with classical Bauhaus color theory and modern web accessibility standards, our platform provides a cohesive color suite. Whether simulating acrylic paint, constructing an accessible design system, or exploring harmonic palettes, understanding these advantages will elevate your workflow.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Part 2: Key Advantages -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#111827] dark:text-white">
            2. Key Advantages: Why Real Color Mixer Outperforms Legacy Digital Tools
          </h3>
          <p>
            Standard digital tools force creators to accept compromises. Real Color Mixer delivers five core advantages designed for accuracy and productivity:
          </p>
          
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#111827] dark:text-white">A. Authentic Subtractive Pigment Optics Without Muddy Grey</h4>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed">
                Standard screen tools linearly average RGB values, turning blue and yellow into muddy brownish-grey (#808040). Real Color Mixer incorporates Kubelka-Munk optical theory, calculating physical absorption and scattering to produce radiant green (#3D933E)—exactly like real physical paint on a palette.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#111827] dark:text-white">B. Dual-Mode Harmonic Theory: Johannes Itten RYB Meets Digital Web</h4>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed">
                Standard software forces creators into digital screen geometry (Red opposite Cyan), ignoring centuries of art education. Real Color Mixer features a dedicated toggle for Johannes Itten's Bauhaus RYB wheel (Red opposite Green, Blue opposite Orange) alongside digital web wheels, letting artists and web designers work without compromise.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#111827] dark:text-white">C. Automated Real-Time WCAG 2.1 Accessibility Validation</h4>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed">
                Modern design demands legal accessibility compliance. Real Color Mixer calculates real-time WCAG 2.1 contrast ratios for every color combination and mixed shade. Instant AA and AAA badges confirm whether black or white text meets legibility criteria on buttons, cards, and interactive elements.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#111827] dark:text-white">D. Frictionless, Privacy-First Architecture Without Account Paywalls</h4>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed">
                Many platforms require paid subscriptions or cloud account logins just to save palettes. Real Color Mixer is completely open, instant, and privacy-respecting, running all calculations locally in your browser with zero sign-ins and zero paywalls.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#ebebeb] dark:border-[#222222] bg-[#f9fafb] dark:bg-[#121212] p-5">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#111827] dark:text-white">E. Developer-Ready Code Exports for Modern CSS and Tailwind</h4>
              <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1aa] leading-relaxed">
                Modern frontend development requires more than copying isolated hexadecimal codes. Our platform generates production-ready CSS variables, Tailwind CSS v4 design tokens, SVG palette assets, and modern CSS color-mix() code in the perceptually uniform OKLCH color space.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Part 3: Professional Uses Across Industries -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#111827] dark:text-white">
            3. Professional Uses & Real-World Applications Across Industries
          </h3>
          <p>
